{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <functional>\n#include <vector>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstdlib>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing lint = long long;\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    lint n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    vector<lint> a(17);\n    a[1] = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i <= 16; ++i)\n        a[i] = a[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n\n    lint ans = LLONG_MAX;\n\n    auto dfs = [&](int pos, lint val, lint cost, auto&& dfs) -> void {\n        if (val == 0) {\n            ans = min(ans, cost);\n            return;\n        }\n        if (pos == 0) return;\n\n        for (int d = -10; d <= 10; ++d) {\n            lint nv = val + d * a[pos];\n            if (nv > 0) {\n                dfs(pos - 1, nv, cost + llabs(d) * pos, dfs);\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int d = -10; d <= 10; ++d) {\n            lint nv = val + d * a[pos];\n            if (nv == 0) {\n                dfs(pos - 1, nv, cost + llabs(d) * pos, dfs);\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int d = 10; d >= -10; --d) {\n            lint nv = val + d * a[pos];\n            if (nv < 0) {\n                dfs(pos - 1, nv, cost + llabs(d) * pos, dfs);\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    };\n\n    dfs(16, n, 0, dfs);\n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        \n        long[] a = new long[17];\n        a[1] = 1;\n        for (int i = 2; i <= 16; ++i) {\n            a[i] = a[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        long[] ans = {Long.MAX_VALUE};\n        \n        // DFS function implemented using a helper class since Java doesn't support recursive lambdas easily\n        DFSHelper dfs = new DFSHelper(a, ans);\n        dfs.dfs(16, n, 0);\n        \n        System.out.println(ans[0]);\n    }\n    \n    static class DFSHelper {\n        long[] a;\n        long[] ans;\n        \n        public DFSHelper(long[] a, long[] ans) {\n            this.a = a;\n            this.ans = ans;\n        }\n        \n        public void dfs(int pos, long val, long cost) {\n            if (val == 0) {\n                ans[0] = Math.min(ans[0], cost);\n                return;\n            }\n            if (pos == 0) return;\n            \n            // First loop: d from -10 to 10, looking for nv > 0\n            for (int d = -10; d <= 10; ++d) {\n                long nv = val + d * a[pos];\n                if (nv > 0) {\n                    dfs(pos - 1, nv, cost + Math.abs(d) * pos);\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n            \n            // Second loop: d from -10 to 10, looking for nv == 0\n            for (int d = -10; d <= 10; ++d) {\n                long nv = val + d * a[pos];\n                if (nv == 0) {\n      